@VINCE_MX:

The author hasn't responded to your suggestions so far, so if consider them critical, you could consider rejecting the contribution.

By the way, I took the time to look into the variable naming issue. Actually, when the stub generates the default codes, it uses different naming conventions for variables depending on the programming language, e.g. snake_case in C and Python, camelCase in C# and Java, and all-lowercase in Haskell. So, I wouldn't consider the letter casing in the statement a significant issue, as long as the variable names used are consistent throughout the sections.
